# `mvcv` moves the *inverse* of C, not its bitwise complement.
#
# Applies to `taligentx/ghidra_csky_ck804` (a fork of `leommxj/ghidra_csky`),
# file `data/languages/16b_data.sinc`, installed at
# `~/Library/ghidra/ghidra_<version>_PUBLIC/Extensions/C-SKY/`.
#
# `psr_cf` is declared `define bitrange psr_cf = psr[0,1]` - one bit, but a
# bitrange is materialised as a whole byte in an expression, so `~psr_cf` is
# 0xFE when C is set and 0xFF when it is clear.  Both are non-zero.  Every
# `mvcv` therefore produced a true value whatever the condition was, and every
# `bez`/`bnez` on a condition the compiler had moved into a register took the
# same branch regardless.  The 32-bit encoding of the same instruction, three
# lines away in `32b_data.sinc`, already had it right as `psr_cf ^ 1`; only the
# 16-bit one was wrong, and the 16-bit one is what the compiler emits.
#
# The disassembly is unaffected, so this is invisible in the listing and in
# every static reading of the decompiler output - `mvcv` decompiles to a
# plausible comparison either way.  It shows up only under execution, and only
# where the branch matters.
#
# Found in `Vocoder_SynthesizeUnvoiced 0x0001AFE0`, whose
#
#     ld.h r3,(r9,0x0) ; cmpnei r3,0x2 ; mvcv r12 ; ... ; bez r4,0x0001b6bc
#
# selects between a per-band energy normalisation (frame class != 2) and a flat
# gain (class == 2).  Every frame in the corpus is class 1, so the radio takes
# the first; the unpatched emulator took the second for all 103 measured calls,
# and the resulting excitation is wrong in every band.
#
# Blast radius on this project's fixtures, measured by regenerating them with
# and without the patch over `tests/fixtures/dm32_arc4_1.frames`:
#
#   `.fwparms`, `.fwenv`, `.fwamps`   identical - the parameter path is clean
#   `.fwpcm`                          31.4% of 57 600 samples differ, worst 57
#                                     LSB against a 1 984 peak, 35.0 dB SNR
#
# so the decoded model parameters were never in doubt and the synthesised audio
# always was.  `tests/fixtures/dm32_arc4_1.fwunvoiced` is regenerated; the PCM
# and everything derived from it - `.fwencbits`, `.fwanalysis` - still predate
# the fix and are marked as such in tools/fw_oracle/README.md.
#
# After editing, recompile the sleigh and start a fresh JVM (analyzeHeadless
# does that per invocation; the GUI needs a restart):
#
#   /opt/homebrew/Cellar/ghidra/<version>/libexec/support/sleigh -a \
#     ~/Library/ghidra/ghidra_<version>_PUBLIC/Extensions/C-SKY/data/languages
#
--- a/16b_data.sinc
+++ b/16b_data.sinc
@@ -103,7 +103,7 @@
 :mvcv i16_r4_rz is i16_optype = 0b01 & i16_4op = 0b1001 & i16_r4_rx_n = 0b0000 & i16_r4_sop = 0b11 & i16_r4_rz {
-    i16_r4_rz = zext(~psr_cf );
+    i16_r4_rz = zext(psr_cf ^ 1);
 }
